WEBVTT

00:00:08.610 --> 00:00:09.470
Rito!

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.810
If you don't stop, I'll—

00:00:12.810 --> 00:00:13.840
Mari-chan!

00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:16.370
Tell me if there's another way.

00:00:17.020 --> 00:00:18.280
Well...

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.460
Closed Today

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:34.460
Sudo's Store

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.050
Fish Sausage

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:56.730
Hup.

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:06.740
Meow, meow.

00:03:12.330 --> 00:03:13.330
Good morning.

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:19.050
How are you feeling?

00:03:20.920 --> 00:03:24.260
I'll bring you dinner tonight.

00:03:33.310 --> 00:03:36.020
Limited Time

00:03:44.780 --> 00:03:48.410
Three, two, one, zero!

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.700
You're right on time again!

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:51.910
Good morning, Rito.

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:54.380
Good morning, Mari.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:56.840
Good morning, Kotoko.

00:03:57.750 --> 00:03:59.420
You have an audition coming up?

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.090
I'm going for a musical next.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.970
I hate how there's never enough time.

00:04:04.510 --> 00:04:06.510
Sometimes, you're Mari-chan, 
the amateur model.

00:04:06.510 --> 00:04:10.470
Other times, you're Mari-chan, the singing 
and dancing idol-in-the-making.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:12.480
But you're actually...

00:04:13.020 --> 00:04:16.190
Mari-chan, the girl who 
makes beautiful clothes!

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:18.980
Your compliments are always welcome.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:23.650
Okay, then... The clothes you make 
are hugely popular in Harajuku.

00:04:23.990 --> 00:04:28.280
Your magical clothes make every 
girl who wears them cute.

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:30.740
You're starting to hit your stride, Kotoko.

00:04:30.740 --> 00:04:32.370
You're Mari-chan the Witch!

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.870
I don't know about that one.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:37.210
Huh?

00:04:42.170 --> 00:04:44.430
Oh, right! Rito-chan, Rito-chan!

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:46.720
What did you talk about with the cat today?

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:49.220
Wait, don't tell me. I'll guess.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.810
Starting today, your grandma's going 
on the Urahara shopping center trip...

00:04:53.810 --> 00:04:59.060
Which means you'll deliver the cat's 
dinner instead of your grandma.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:00.270
Is that right?

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:01.730
Correct.

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:06.160
All right! I won a prize!

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:08.740
What about the store? Is it closed?

00:05:09.120 --> 00:05:12.450
Yeah. Only locals come to our store,

00:05:12.450 --> 00:05:14.080
and we're never busy on weekends.

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:16.000
Is that right?

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:19.540
I wonder what people who live 
in Harajuku do on weekends.

00:05:19.540 --> 00:05:24.550
Normally you imagine people coming 
to Harajuku to shop and eat, right?

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:28.510
I'm sure the people who live there 
don't go sightseeing every day.

00:05:28.510 --> 00:05:31.100
It's so strange that you're from Harajuku.

00:05:31.100 --> 00:05:34.310
It does seem like it's 
Halloween every day there.

00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:37.100
My neighborhood's so quiet, I can't sleep.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:39.560
My neighborhood's full of houses and temples.

00:05:39.560 --> 00:05:42.270
Even in the middle of the day, 
it's like the whole neighborhood's asleep.

00:05:42.270 --> 00:05:45.280
Don't you ever feel like 
the tourists are too loud?

00:05:45.280 --> 00:05:48.530
Nope. And I met you two 
because of what Harajuku is.

00:05:49.780 --> 00:05:51.160
Rito-chan, I love you!

00:05:51.160 --> 00:05:52.450
I love you so much!

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:53.950
It's time.

00:05:53.950 --> 00:05:54.830
Let's open.

00:05:55.450 --> 00:05:56.290
Okay.

00:05:59.580 --> 00:06:02.460
I just love weekends.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:04.090
You can do whatever you want all day.

00:06:04.380 --> 00:06:06.420
I can't believe I get paid for this.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:09.090
I wish I could spend every day at Park.

00:06:09.090 --> 00:06:11.550
If only spring break would last forever...

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:13.510
Wait, no!

00:06:13.510 --> 00:06:15.600
I don't want to be a high 
school student forever!

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:18.140
I forgot that I don't like high school!

00:06:18.140 --> 00:06:19.020
Neither do I.

00:06:19.020 --> 00:06:20.400
Don't worry.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.650
If any of us get held back, it'll be me.

00:06:23.400 --> 00:06:25.440
Is that a summer design?

00:06:25.440 --> 00:06:26.400
Yeah.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:29.200
What do you think? I drew a few sketches.

00:06:29.200 --> 00:06:32.120
Rito, are you Karl Lagerfeld's 
secret love child?

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.330
They're so cute! I wanna try
them on! I want them all!

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:39.370
It'd be nice to see all kinds 
of girls wear our clothes.

00:06:39.370 --> 00:06:40.040
Yeah!

00:06:40.040 --> 00:06:41.920
Every girl in Harajuku.

00:06:42.920 --> 00:06:45.590
Rito-chan, have you come up 
with any designs for sweets?

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:48.470
Like, special limited edition sweets!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:51.430
I'm still working on that, 
but here's what I'm thinking.

00:06:52.220 --> 00:06:54.300
That looks great.

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:58.270
It just needs a bit of a Japanese touch, 
since that's popular right now.

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:00.770
I know! We could put 
Japanese sugar candies on it!

00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:04.610
And how about Japanese sugar 
cookies shaped like bears?

00:07:04.610 --> 00:07:06.730
If you can design that, Rito,

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:09.360
you'll have overshot genius 
and crossed over into crazy.

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:14.410
Ooh! Are you Rito-chan the Witch?

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.040
Welcome.

00:07:25.210 --> 00:07:26.960
Welcome.

00:07:26.960 --> 00:07:27.880
Wow!

00:07:28.130 --> 00:07:33.010
He's supremely unique, even 
for fashion-forward Harajuku.

00:07:33.590 --> 00:07:38.520
As far as he's concerned, our 
clothes might seem unique to him.

00:07:38.520 --> 00:07:44.480
Either way, we can let Mari-chan, the 
goddess of customer service, handle it.

00:07:44.730 --> 00:07:46.320
Can I help you find anything?

00:07:46.320 --> 00:07:47.360
Indeed.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:53.570
I'm searching for creative individuals 
who can create something from nothing.

00:07:53.570 --> 00:07:54.490
Of course.

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:56.120
I know what you mean.

00:07:56.120 --> 00:07:58.830
Living things must experience all emotions,

00:07:58.830 --> 00:08:01.790
from joy to sadness, and some 
degree of satisfaction, too.

00:08:01.790 --> 00:08:05.580
I believe that is art.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:07.290
I see!

00:08:07.540 --> 00:08:10.960
Artistic fashion and food 
to satisfy my tastes...

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:13.550
This store has it all!

00:08:13.550 --> 00:08:15.300
We get that a lot.

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.560
This store is a physical 
representation of our dreams.

00:08:19.560 --> 00:08:21.730
We hope you like it.

00:08:24.230 --> 00:08:26.310
I do like it! Yes!

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:30.860
So, what are you looking for today?

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:32.190
Everything.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:34.530
Everything, including your talent.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:36.530
Well, thank you!

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.910
Ah, I knew I'd find it in Urahara.

00:08:39.910 --> 00:08:45.710
I found what I needed and what I've been 
looking for in the back streets of Japan.

00:08:45.710 --> 00:08:48.250
Our store can be hard to find,

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:49.800
so I'm glad you were able to find it.

00:08:50.300 --> 00:08:54.840
Now, everything. I'll take everything.

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:56.760
One moment, please.

00:08:57.010 --> 00:09:00.350
I'll be right back! Right back!

00:09:00.350 --> 00:09:02.100
Thank you!

00:09:03.020 --> 00:09:04.350
What was that?

00:09:04.350 --> 00:09:05.810
Who knows?

00:09:05.810 --> 00:09:09.190
Mari-chan, I'm amazed you understood him.

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:10.610
I didn't.

00:09:10.610 --> 00:09:12.110
I wonder who he is.

00:09:12.650 --> 00:09:13.440
Yeah.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:19.490
What is that?

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:20.830
It's an alarm.

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:22.040
Be careful.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:24.580
What was that?

00:09:24.580 --> 00:09:25.870
A UFO invasion?

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:28.830
Then we'll have to throw 
them a welcome party.

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.000
Kotoko's right.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:32.460
What?

00:09:32.460 --> 00:09:33.210
Huh?

00:09:46.230 --> 00:09:48.940
<i>Once again, just after noon today,</i>

00:09:48.940 --> 00:09:51.730
<i>mysterious flying objects 
invaded Japanese skies,</i>

00:09:51.730 --> 00:09:54.280
<i>erasing buildings one after another.</i>

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.070
<i>According to international reports,</i>

00:09:56.070 --> 00:10:00.950
<i>the flying objects have appeared not 
just in Japan, but across the globe.</i>

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.950
It really is a UFO invasion!

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:06.000
This is amazing!

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:07.500
It's like a movie!

00:10:07.500 --> 00:10:10.880
I always wished something 
like this would happen.

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:12.130
And it actually did!

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:14.460
Is this an early April Fool's joke?

00:10:14.460 --> 00:10:17.470
Since it's a UFO invasion, maybe 
they're celebrating Independence Day.

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:20.640
Or perhaps it's a nation-wide prank?

00:10:20.640 --> 00:10:23.010
You can't expect me to believe this.

00:10:23.010 --> 00:10:25.470
No, it's real.

00:10:26.060 --> 00:10:27.390
Here's Tokyo Tower.

00:10:27.390 --> 00:10:29.440
It's too big to be a prank.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:32.230
This must be costing them a ton.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:36.150
Or maybe your smartphone 
and tablet are broken.

00:10:36.150 --> 00:10:40.860
I guess it's possible that someone 
could've hacked them.

00:10:41.410 --> 00:10:42.910
Let's see what's going on outside.

00:10:43.330 --> 00:10:47.160
The neighborhood must be talking 
about a story this big.

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:49.040
You're right. Let's go!

00:10:49.040 --> 00:10:51.380
This truly is a close 
encounter of the third kind.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.750
Wow, everyone's so surprised.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:58.220
They're too good to be extras.

00:10:58.220 --> 00:11:00.380
Looks like it isn't a prank.

00:11:00.680 --> 00:11:03.470
That can't be. There's no way. It's a lie.

00:11:03.470 --> 00:11:05.350
I don't believe it!

00:11:06.430 --> 00:11:07.430
Look at that.

00:11:07.430 --> 00:11:12.900
World News

00:11:07.730 --> 00:11:09.140
<i>As we've already reported,</i>

00:11:09.140 --> 00:11:13.560
<i>the mysterious organisms flying 
above Japan are erasing buildings.</i>

00:11:13.560 --> 00:11:15.480
<i>We're receiving video 
of the events right now.</i>

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:17.480
<i>It's the Kaminarimon in Asakusa.</i>

00:11:19.110 --> 00:11:20.320
<i>It disappeared!</i>

00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:23.160
<i>Tokyo Tower has disappeared 
without a trace!</i>

00:11:23.160 --> 00:11:26.660
<i>The defense force deployed by the 
government is already on the move</i>

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.870
<i>and will commence its attack shortly.</i>

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:32.750
<i>The International Defense 
Headquarters has announced that</i>

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.540
<i>they're calling these organisms "Scoopers,"</i>

00:11:34.540 --> 00:11:38.090
<i>because of the way they "scoop" 
buildings out of existence.</i>

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:40.760
<i>I repeat, the International 
Defense Headquarters...</i>

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:40.760
Scoopers...

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.550
Why? What are they doing?

00:11:43.550 --> 00:11:44.390
I don't believe this.

00:11:44.640 --> 00:11:46.810
I refuse to believe this!

00:11:48.560 --> 00:11:50.930
My parents are telling me to come home.

00:11:50.930 --> 00:11:52.060
So are mine.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:56.360
They sent me a bunch of messages 
telling me to come home.

00:11:57.730 --> 00:12:00.400
I hope my grandma's okay.

00:12:00.400 --> 00:12:04.160
Where did the Urahara 
shopping center trip go?

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.370
Hakone.

00:12:05.370 --> 00:12:07.080
The mysterious organisms...

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:12.290
no, the Scoopers seem to be stealing 
symbolic Japanese landmarks.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.080
I wonder if they'll take Hakone.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:16.250
That's a good old cultural spot.

00:12:16.250 --> 00:12:17.800
I'm sure it'll be fine.

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:21.170
Yeah! That's what I was 
trying to say, Rito-chan!

00:12:21.170 --> 00:12:24.680
Thanks. Are your families okay?

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:26.930
Yeah, mine's fine.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:27.810
So is mine.

00:12:27.810 --> 00:12:29.260
Rito, what about your parents?

00:12:29.930 --> 00:12:33.230
I haven't talked to them since the divorce.

00:12:34.270 --> 00:12:37.110
Hey, there's a new report.

00:12:37.310 --> 00:12:40.300
<i>The Scoopers are heading toward Harajuku.</i>

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:42.740
<i>Their current expected time 
of arrival is exactly 2:00 PM.</i>

00:12:43.030 --> 00:12:45.030
<i>They will be arriving shortly.</i>

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:48.160
<i>If you're in Harajuku now, 
please calmly evacuate the area.</i>

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:49.370
<i>I repeat...</i>

00:12:50.790 --> 00:12:52.660
They're coming here!

00:12:52.910 --> 00:12:55.000
What an awful weekend.

00:12:55.000 --> 00:12:55.870
What should we do?

00:12:56.170 --> 00:12:59.250
I want to see them, but 
we should evacuate, right?

00:12:59.250 --> 00:13:03.380
If they're arriving at 2:00 PM and 
coming from where Tokyo Tower stood,

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:08.800
they're coming through Roppongi and 
Nishi-Azabu, which is basically due east, so...

00:13:09.220 --> 00:13:12.980
We should run west toward Yoyogi Park.

00:13:12.980 --> 00:13:15.440
I wouldn't want to run into them.

00:13:19.270 --> 00:13:20.400
I wonder why.

00:13:21.230 --> 00:13:22.820
What's wrong, Rito-chan?

00:13:23.990 --> 00:13:25.320
I don't...

00:13:28.950 --> 00:13:30.990
I don't want to leave Harajuku.

00:13:31.490 --> 00:13:33.450
I don't know why, but neither do I.

00:13:33.450 --> 00:13:36.920
Even though I'm scared, for some 
reason, I don't want to, either.

00:13:37.330 --> 00:13:42.380
Then why don't we go somewhere 
culturally insignificant in Harajuku?

00:13:42.380 --> 00:13:43.340
Great idea.

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.220
Like...

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:46.180
Hey.

00:13:46.590 --> 00:13:48.260
Why don't we go back to Park?

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:53.970
Some adults say that the store's part 
of Harajuku's youth culture,

00:13:54.390 --> 00:13:56.310
but Park is where we belong.

00:14:06.030 --> 00:14:06.990
They're here!

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:08.700
There's so many of them.

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:11.580
Shouldn't you be more shocked 
to see your first UFO?

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:14.750
Oh, this isn't the first 
time I've seen a UFO.

00:14:14.750 --> 00:14:16.500
I saw one when I was at—

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.790
Kotoko, you can tell us later.

00:14:18.790 --> 00:14:21.040
I'm really confused right now.

00:14:21.040 --> 00:14:24.250
I might even throw a welcome 
party for the Scoopers!

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:29.640
What's going on?

00:14:29.640 --> 00:14:32.550
No, what's going to happen?

00:14:43.320 --> 00:14:44.650
It's so cute!

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:45.940
I won't deny that,

00:14:45.940 --> 00:14:49.150
but shouldn't we assume that this 
is related to the Scoopers?

00:14:50.280 --> 00:14:51.620
It's making a noise.

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:56.290
She's so cute!

00:14:56.290 --> 00:14:58.660
I won't deny that, but...

00:15:01.080 --> 00:15:02.500
A girl?

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:04.290
Yes, indeed.

00:15:04.290 --> 00:15:06.550
It's an alien girl!

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:07.630
I'm not an alien.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:13.050
I was captured by the aliens called "Scoopers" 
that they're talking about on the news, indeed.

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:14.350
Captured?

00:15:14.350 --> 00:15:15.930
Really? That's great!

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:17.350
You escaped!

00:15:17.350 --> 00:15:19.420
Did they experiment on you?

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:21.600
You're not hurt, are you? Are you okay?

00:15:21.980 --> 00:15:24.020
Yes, indeed.

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:25.570
Where's your family?

00:15:25.570 --> 00:15:28.530
My dad and mom are in America.

00:15:28.530 --> 00:15:32.700
I was kidnapped by the Scoopers 
while I was in America.

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:35.240
When? How did you escape?

00:15:35.240 --> 00:15:41.250
I, Ebifurya, can answer that 
question for Misa-sama.

00:15:41.750 --> 00:15:43.290
It's a talking fried shrimp!

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:44.380
The name's Ebifurya.

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:47.250
I can't handle this anymore.

00:15:47.630 --> 00:15:50.010
A talking fried shrimp?

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.340
My name is Ebifurya.

00:15:52.630 --> 00:15:54.680
I am Ebifurya.

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:58.140
The Scoopers treated me 
as something like a pet.

00:15:58.140 --> 00:16:00.810
However, now I'm Misa-sama's pet.

00:16:00.810 --> 00:16:05.020
As such, I'm an ally of Misa-sama 
and all creatures of Earth.

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:05.690
Yes!

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:06.770
He's on our side!

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:09.530
Maybe we can be friends!

00:16:09.530 --> 00:16:11.700
What are the Scoopers?

00:16:12.360 --> 00:16:17.530
The creatures you call "Scoopers" 
have no culture of their own

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:20.540
and lack the power to create it.

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:24.540
Their culture consists entirely of cultures 
they've stolen from other planets.

00:16:24.540 --> 00:16:29.920
And their current target 
is this planet you live on...

00:16:30.960 --> 00:16:33.050
Earth!

00:16:33.050 --> 00:16:37.970
They kidnapped me because they thought 
a human could create culture for them.

00:16:37.970 --> 00:16:43.020
But thanks to me, Ebifurya, 
we were able to escape.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:44.980
Thank you, indeed.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:48.110
I appreciate the moving story, 
but I have another question.

00:16:48.110 --> 00:16:50.020
What's going to happen to us?

00:16:50.020 --> 00:16:51.530
If you know the answer, tell us.

00:16:51.820 --> 00:16:55.910
They want only one thing: culture.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:58.030
The power of imagination.

00:16:58.030 --> 00:17:00.160
In other words, this planet's creativity.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:02.910
And they plan to steal it all.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:04.870
But what about us?

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:06.380
What's going to happen to us?

00:17:06.380 --> 00:17:10.500
Doesn't that mean they're 
thieves? Culture thieves?

00:17:10.500 --> 00:17:12.880
Yeah, we should report them to the police!

00:17:12.880 --> 00:17:15.180
Mari, we should head to Park first.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.140
Misa-chan, come with us.

00:17:16.390 --> 00:17:18.010
Yes, indeed.

00:17:18.010 --> 00:17:19.100
We're taking her with us?

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.850
We can't leave her here.

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:28.860
Hide.

00:17:35.530 --> 00:17:37.240
It's so big and cute!

00:17:37.660 --> 00:17:38.870
Stand back, everyone.

00:17:38.870 --> 00:17:41.540
Use this, indeed.

00:17:45.040 --> 00:17:47.960
I stole it from the Scoopers' ship.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:50.790
I'm sure these Amatsumara 
will be useful, indeed!

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:52.920
Amatsumara?

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.470
That's what the Scoopers called them.

00:17:55.470 --> 00:17:58.140
Amatsumara are the physical 
embodiment of imagination.

00:17:58.140 --> 00:18:03.270
They're products from another planet 
that the Scoopers couldn't use,

00:18:03.270 --> 00:18:05.810
since they lack imagination.

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:09.020
However, as imaginative residents of Earth,

00:18:09.020 --> 00:18:13.480
you'll be able to use the Amatsumara 
to fight against the Scoopers.

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.320
Let's defend Harajuku.

00:18:16.570 --> 00:18:19.030
I've always wanted to do this!

00:18:19.030 --> 00:18:20.740
I have no idea what's going on!

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:32.590
You've been chosen by the Amatsumara.

00:18:32.590 --> 00:18:36.800
I know you'll be able to 
protect the city, indeed.

00:18:40.010 --> 00:18:41.100
We have to try.

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:41.760
Yeah.

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:43.970
What? You can't be serious!

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:46.430
I believe you called yourself Rito-san?

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:48.560
Your movements are constantly shifting.

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:50.400
Imagine yourself fighting.

00:18:50.400 --> 00:18:52.690
Yes, as though you were drawing a picture.

00:18:53.690 --> 00:18:56.280
Your speed will serve as a weapon.

00:18:56.280 --> 00:18:58.150
Imagine myself fighting...

00:18:58.150 --> 00:19:01.780
Kotoko-san, you'll provide 
logistical support.

00:19:02.320 --> 00:19:05.040
You should be able to implement strategies.

00:19:05.580 --> 00:19:08.330
Yay! My tablet's been upgraded!

00:19:08.330 --> 00:19:12.880
Mari-san, your cannon is capable 
of firing finishing blows.

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:15.340
Use it when the time is right.

00:19:15.340 --> 00:19:17.010
I can't do that!

00:19:17.340 --> 00:19:20.340
Misa-chan, it's dangerous 
out here. You should hide.

00:19:20.340 --> 00:19:22.340
Okay, indeed.

00:19:22.850 --> 00:19:23.760
Let's go.

00:19:23.760 --> 00:19:24.260
Yeah.

00:19:24.260 --> 00:19:25.930
Are you serious?

00:19:26.930 --> 00:19:28.390
I'll draw them to me.

00:19:28.390 --> 00:19:30.810
Kotoko, where should I go?

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:34.150
You'll cause minimal damage in Yoyogi Park.

00:19:34.150 --> 00:19:37.820
Gather the UFOs there so 
Mari-chan can mop them up.

00:19:37.820 --> 00:19:38.780
Okay.

00:19:38.780 --> 00:19:40.900
But I hate cleaning!

00:19:40.900 --> 00:19:41.990
Rito-san!

00:19:41.990 --> 00:19:44.370
The UFOs are fast. Be careful.

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:44.870
Got it.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:48.580
Mari-san, you'll have 
trouble aiming at first.

00:19:48.580 --> 00:19:51.620
If you can just land one 
shot when the time comes—

00:19:51.620 --> 00:19:53.630
I told you, I can't!

00:19:53.630 --> 00:19:56.300
It's okay. I know you can do it, Mari-chan.

00:19:56.300 --> 00:19:57.880
Mari-chan the Witch!

00:19:57.880 --> 00:20:00.260
I told you, I'm not a fan of that one!

00:20:00.760 --> 00:20:02.510
Come on. This way.

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:14.400
<i>Rito-chan!</i>

00:20:14.770 --> 00:20:18.070
Don't accidentally get caught 
in Mari-chan's bazooka blast.

00:20:18.070 --> 00:20:20.240
Is she really telling me to shoot?

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:22.990
Apparently, your bazooka 
will take aim for you.

00:20:23.990 --> 00:20:26.450
What's going on? What's going on?

00:20:26.450 --> 00:20:28.040
It locked on.

00:20:28.330 --> 00:20:30.700
<i>Here we go, Rito-chan.</i>

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.250
<i>Dodge the shots!</i>

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:38.170
Bazooka firing in three, two, one...

00:20:38.170 --> 00:20:43.010
I can't!

00:20:49.100 --> 00:20:50.390
Bull's-eye!

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:51.890
I'm not happy about that...

00:20:55.440 --> 00:20:57.360
Amazing, indeed.

00:20:58.020 --> 00:20:59.530
Donuts?

00:21:00.900 --> 00:21:03.570
All right! I won a prize!

00:21:03.570 --> 00:21:05.410
Is this supposed to be our reward?

00:21:08.240 --> 00:21:09.280
<i>It's a missile!</i>

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:11.080
<i>This isn't a Scooper missile!</i>

00:21:11.080 --> 00:21:12.250
What is it, then?

00:21:12.710 --> 00:21:15.080
It's an International Defense Force bomb!

00:21:15.080 --> 00:21:17.580
At this rate, we'll all die!

00:21:17.580 --> 00:21:18.990
This is serious!

00:21:21.870 --> 00:21:24.060
<i>I want to protect the city.</i>

00:21:24.660 --> 00:21:26.240
<i>I want to stay here.</i>

00:21:26.820 --> 00:21:28.540
<i>This place is everything to me.</i>

00:21:33.410 --> 00:21:35.980
Their self-defense system has activated!

00:21:37.570 --> 00:21:38.510
Is that...

00:21:38.810 --> 00:21:40.500
It's the parfait we were talking about!

00:21:40.500 --> 00:21:41.970
It looks delicious!

00:21:41.970 --> 00:21:43.720
Yeah, it does look delicious.

00:21:43.720 --> 00:21:46.480
But this is no time to eat!

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:28.110
Misa-sama, this is the 
discovery of the century!

00:23:28.110 --> 00:23:29.450
What, what? What is it?

00:23:29.450 --> 00:23:32.620
When you eat salted popcorn 
and caramel corn together,

00:23:32.620 --> 00:23:35.060
it becomes salted caramel corn!

00:23:35.610 --> 00:23:37.060
Of course it does.
